    "PROVENANCE — READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING ANYTHING BELOW.",
    "",
    "These are NOT captured from a Microsoft 365 tenant. They are hand-built to the shape of the",
    "Microsoft Graph `message` resource as Microsoft documents it, using the field names, casing and",
    "value formats from that published schema. They were written this way because capturing real",
    "payloads requires a credential, and __mj.Credential is empty on our host — the very gap this",
    "work exists to close.",
    "",
    "WHAT THAT MEANS FOR ANY DEMO USING THEM. The engine, the Graph mapper, participant resolution,",
    "direction inference, threading and the watermark are all exercised for real. What is NOT proven",
    "is that Microsoft returns exactly these shapes for these fields. The first live run is still the",
    "first live run, and the honest thing is to say so rather than let a green demo imply otherwise.",
    "",
    "Every address is on example.com / example.org, which RFC 2606 reserves precisely so sample data",
    "cannot reach a real mailbox.",
    "",
    "Fields present here that the mapper does NOT read (isRead, importance, webLink, hasAttachments,",
    "internetMessageId, parentFolderId, changeKey) are kept deliberately: a real Graph response",
    "carries them, and stripping them would make the fixture agree with our mapper rather than with",
    "Microsoft. NormalizedItem.Raw preserves the whole payload, so they should be here."
